Hlarf is the bluish-skinned half-giant who speaks for the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] to outsiders. He stands a head taller than the men around him and holds court at a table in the gang's back room at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|The Crowded Flea]]. He was the one who told Johnny that if [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] found him interesting he might meet him the next evening on [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Pier 54]]. He fights with his fists, and one punch is enough to put a person on the ground.

Hlarf and the gang's other members are werecreatures; the ones the Party saw in the back room turned into boars, rats and a crocodile. When the Party appeared in the room by magic one night, Hlarf was there, and he helped finish them. Three of the Party died in the room and the fourth fled out the window.

After the killing, the gang stripped the dead and dumped Johnny, Benny and Argyle in the river, and took the group's company car and gear.

The Party killed Hlarf in revenge, in a [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] alley in the small hours, where [[Aut]] told them he would stop drunk after a meeting. [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] put a coin through his head. His car, a 632 Chorath Aventine, went to the Party.

He kept a diary, three months of which the Party recovered: coins skimmed from the Roundhat rackets, some competent poetry, and a meeting inside [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]] with someone he did not name.
